  "live_records": {
    "q-15857": {
      "dom_id": "step-q15857",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221931/assets/33070b4b871552c4c45f21f0885cbce45ff65eb278cb000e68c91adfc2ab004c.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $16$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(16,0)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=16.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
