    "q-105916": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105916",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $\\frac{1}{3}$ centered at the origin?",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
