    "q-79163": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79163",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(-5,-2)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(-5,-2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -5,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
