    "q-79192": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79192",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221931/assets/6b77b1b8a61b5ec7306fbc0b3d70618e7fdce2237bdcbfd017c23c01b80f2979.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-4,5)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(-1,5)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-4,5).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-79192-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4",
