    "q-106693": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106693",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(5,-3)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(5,-3).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
